  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multisectoral Humanitarian Response at Turkish Borders</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following the successful implementation of the Multisectoral Humanitarian Response at Turkish Borders project, IOM&#x2019;s Phase V of its humanitarian assistance programming to continue to expand support to migrants in irregular situations in T&#xfc;rkiye&#x2019;s Western Border particularly those intercepted/rescued at sea by the Turkish Coast Guard in the Aegean Region and/or apprehended or pushed back to T&#xfc;rkiye on the north-western border (hereinafter migrants). Through multi-sectoral humanitarian assistance, IOM aims to meet migrants&#x2019; basic, protection and medical needs. These assistances are planned to be in the form of providing food items, non-food items, Mental Health and Psychosocial Support, including Psychological First Aid, basic medical support and assistance, and referrals to specialized mid-and long-term service providers. IOM aims continue its humanitarian assistance programming in the Aegean region and the north-western border.</narrative>
  </description>
